    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d184">

                <pb facs="0229" n="1063" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1063"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/10340</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Sharp</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-10-01T12:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 1, 1918—noon.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 8.48 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5256. War Trade Board [from McFadden]:</p>
                <p>No. 465. Referring Department’s 5506, of September 4, 3 p.m., your 287.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>We have presented content of above telegram as instructed. Ministry
                        Blockade is in accord with your views as expressed therein <pb facs="0230"
                            n="1064" xml:id="pg1064"/> and in your letter of July l,<anchor n="1"
                            xml:id="d184-f1"/> with exceptions hereafter noted, and will from now on
                        present cases covering Switzerland, Spain, and Morocco to enemy trade
                        license committee in Paris for its consideration and action.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>The Ministry of Blockade will submit cases covering trade between
                        individuals and firms in French territory and— <list>
                            <label>(<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>)</label>
                            <item>Enemy persons or firms;</item>
                            <label>(<hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>)</label>
                            <item>Individuals or firms appearing on the <hi rendition="#italic"
                                    >liste noire officielle;</hi>
                            </item>
                            <label>(<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>)</label>
                            <item>Individuals or firms appearing on the <hi rendition="#italic"
                                    >liste noire confidentielle.</hi>
                            </item>
                        </list>
                    </item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>The Ministry of Blockade will not submit cases of trading with above
                        persons or firms when the transaction is one which was started before such
                        persons or firms were included upon the various black lists or [became]
                        suspect. Licenses for such transactions, which are known as <hi
                            rendition="#italic">affaires en cours</hi>, will be granted only by the
                        French Commission Inter-Ministerielle des Listes Noires.</item>
                    <label>4.</label>
                    <item>The Ministry of Blockade is unable to answer at the present time the
                        question as to submitting cases of trading between the French Government and
                        persons mentioned in paragraphs (<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>), (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">b</hi>), and (<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>) above,
                        as they do not know whether the Government is still making purchases or
                        doing business of this sort. Blockade will advise us regarding this point
                        after consultation with French Ministries of Armament and Commerce, when we
                        will inform you. McFadden.</item>
                </list>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sharp</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
